{"entryId":"1761","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1761:1","sourceSha256":"2d835b6b2fc46214e5bbad1687be545c7fcbb7aade1cf4ea58a2cecdd98305fb","englishSha256":"a060c62550faa565c006efa1ac49c73504b80d156992de8a058de988df6678e1","citations":[{"id":"1761:1:citation-01","he":[83,141],"en":[139,192],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Eikhah_Rabbah_1.47"},"reference":"Eikhah Rabbah 1:47","assessment":"Eikhah Rabbah names Miriam, narrates the approach over carpets and mentions her allowance after Yehoshua’s death. This supports the name and literary description of wealth.","evidence":[{"reference":"Eikhah Rabbah 1:47","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Eikhah_Rabbah_1.47"},"witness":"Midrash Rabbah -- TE"}]},{"id":"1761:1:citation-02","he":[143,243],"en":[388,396],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_18a.10"},"reference":"Yoma 18a:10","assessment":"Yoma records payment and appointment. Rashi calls her a wealthy widow and places the money after betrothal, consistent with before the marriage was completed.","evidence":[{"reference":"Yoma 18a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_18a.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Rashi on Yoma 18a:10:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Yoma_18a.10.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Yevamot 61a:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yevamot_61a.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1761:1:citation-03","he":[245,379],"en":[412,425],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Yoma_18a.10.1"},"reference":"Tosafot on Yoma 18a:10:1","assessment":"Tosafot explicitly distinguish the rulers with the high-priest rationale, as does Tosafot Yeshanim. The checked Rashi describes the appointment without the distinction. Kiddushin names a high priest king and records the killings. Heilprin’s reference is near the start of the chapter HaOmer, not the tractate.","evidence":[{"reference":"Tos